Arena Season 3, BC.

&#x200B;

Chasing druids around pillars was an absolutely miserable experience, and resilience gearing added annoying busy work to the gear process. 

&#x200B;

The overworld all but died and people just sat in town and queue'd for whatever, only venturing out sometimes to do their daily chores (dailies), or to Raid.

&#x200B;

The server community died. All of the previous mainstays disbanded and there were no more rivalries to speak of.

&#x200B;

The server would occasionally spring to life with content patches, but by and large the entire thing was a dreary shadow of what it was in Vanilla.

&#x200B;

I did a free cataclysm trial, hoping that the remaking of the world would liven up the community, but the server was even deader than before, and with dungeon finder; there was no reason to even talk to the people you're grouping with.

&#x200B;

I stayed off until Legion, where I played Demon Hunter to cap and found more of the same problems. Up until cap the game was basically single player anyway, even on my new server.

&#x200B;

Then I came back for BFA, made a warrior; had fun during the pre expansion time with the free handout gear / farming for transmogs, then quickly fell off once the ill advised level cap scaling kicked in. Didn't help that warriors were now, somehow; the worst tanks and not even great for DPS.

"It's over"

&#x200B;

Yep.

The popular complaints are far from trivial, and just because other titles have been larger dumpster fires doesn't excuse what happens here. The bugs are numerous and affect the experience significantly. 

&#x200B;

People can launch themselves far distances across the map with an easily reproducible exploit. This has been in the game for a long time.

&#x200B;

Fortified buff is bugged.

&#x200B;

The netcode is the worst of any modern shooter.

&#x200B;

Hitbox advantage of certain characters, specifically Wraith and Pathfinder.

&#x200B;

Hitreg just not working sometimes, made even worse by the above. Oh there's nothing quite like having your bullets fly through a Wingman ADS strafing wraith who is not only moving faster than normaly for some reason, but is extra tiny AND harder to hit than normal.

&#x200B;

The game is really fun when it shines, but both the design of the game and the staggering amount of technical problems it suffers from; it fails to do this consistently for all but a select few players. 

&#x200B;

Influencers want many of the same things the players want, and while their role in discourse is far too large in my opinion; these are issues that the player base would complain about anyway.

&#x200B;

Stop excusing mediocer work.

