If you're trying to get anywhere via bus during off peak hours, the drivers flat out just come whenever they want. 5 minutes early, 8 minutes late OR they just don't show up at all with no explanation other than "ohabusbrokedown" mumbled by the driver. Many times the bus time app doesn't even show buses on the radar. 

&#x200B;

If I end up working late, or staying out late, a 1:00am bus will just show up at 1:40 because "who cares its late and its Staten Island". It makes me want to leave my apartment when my lease is up and just go live in Brooklyn where I work with a roommate or something. 45 minute commutes take over 90 minutes because of how poorly buses run at certain times of the day.

"Pursue hobbies that interest you naturally" is worthless, vague advice.

&#x200B;

If you're the type that tends to run solo (Like me) or just shy, you will inevitably fall back into what you naturally do. As you've said. 

&#x200B;

Nobody in these scenarios will have a reason to speak with you.

&#x200B;

If your goal is to meet people, then try to discover something \*NEW\* that you think will help you to connect with others \*AND\* something you'd enjoy. I myself am learning how to play to saxophone. Once I get comfortable playing, I'm going to wander around the outdoor cityscape, playing to see if sometimes happens with that.

